{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Bandage_Up","to":"Bandage Up"},{"from":"Fiend_Fire","to":"Fiend Fire"},{"from":"All_for_One","to":"All for One"},{"from":"Spirit_Shield","to":"Spirit Shield"},{"from":"Become_Almighty","to":"Become Almighty"},{"from":"Limit_Break","to":"Limit Break"},{"from":"Dark_Shackles","to":"Dark Shackles"},{"from":"Bowling_Bash","to":"Bowling Bash"},{"from":"Fire_Breathing","to":"Fire Breathing"}],"pages":{"2262":{"pageid":2262,"ns":0,"title":"All for One","revisions":[{"revid":56311,"parentid":55261,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = All for One\n| Image       = Blue-AllforOne.png\n| Color       = Blue\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Deal (10;14) damage.<br>Put all cost 0 cards from your discard pile into your hand.\n}}\n{{C|All for One}} is a 2 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 10 (14 if upgraded) damage, and it will put all 0-cost cards from your discard pile into your hand. 0 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' does not have to be the base {{Icon|BE}}-cost of that card, as long as it costs 0 while in the discard pile, it will be put in hand by this card.\n\n{{C|All for One}} will not put all 0-cost cards from your discard pile into your hand if that amount would exceed the hand size limit. In that case, it will take the cards in the order they appear in the discard pile until your hand is full.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{C|All for One}} will not count as part of the hand anymore by the time it brings back 0 {{Icon|BE}}-cost cards, meaning it does not count towards the hand size limit.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* It synergizes with every 0-cost card, all of which that belong to the Defect listed below:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Beam Cell}}, {{C|Claw}}, {{C|Go for the Eyes}}, {{C|Steam Barrier}}, {{C|TURBO}}, {{C|FTL}}, and {{C|Overclock}}. \n* If not yet {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by playing them, {{C|Boot Sequence}}, {{C|Chill}}, {{C|Fission}}, {{C|Reboot}}, and {{C|Seek}}.\n* If upgraded, {{C|Dualcast}}, {{C|Zap}}, and {{C|Recycle}}.  \n* If upgraded and not yet {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by playing them, {{C|Double Energy}} and {{C|White Noise}}\n* {{C|Streamline}} and {{C|Force Field}}, as long as they have been reduced to 0 cost already.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Cards with no concrete {{Icon|BE}}-cost, such as {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Statuses}}, and X-cost cards will never be put in hand by {{C|All for One}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Scrape and All For One cards now correctly work with cards that set cost to 0 until played.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1827":{"pageid":1827,"ns":0,"title":"Armaments","revisions":[{"revid":56323,"parentid":55624,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Armaments\n| Image       = Red-Armaments.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain 5 {{KW|Block}}.<br>{{KW|Upgrade}} (a card;all cards) in your hand for the rest of combat.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block, Upgrade\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Keyword Infobox|Upgrade}}\n{{C|Armaments}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 5 {{KW|Block}}, and allows you to select one card in your hand to upgrade. If {{C|Armaments}} is upgraded, it upgrades your entire hand instead. These upgrades last until the end of combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Can repeatedly upgrade {{C|Searing Blow}} for the duration of combat.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Using {{C|Armaments}} to {{KW|Upgrade}} a card that changes {{Icon|RE}}-cost when {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} will immediately set it to that {{Icon|RE}}-cost. This also applies if the card previously had its cost randomized by {{BD|Confused}} or {{P|Snecko Oil}}, unless its cost initially got randomized to 0, in which case it remains 0 when upgraded.\n** A {{C|Blood for Blood}} that costs more than 0 {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' will always go down by 1 in {{Icon|RE}}-cost when {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}}, regardless of what cost it was randomized to.\n** For example, if an unupgraded {{C|Corruption}} is randomized to 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost, upgrading it with {{C|Armaments}} will increase its cost to 2.\n\n* Although {{C|Burn}} has an upgraded version, it cannot be upgraded by the player, and is therefore unaffected by {{C|Armaments}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Having played {{C|Apotheosis}} or having your hand {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} by {{P|Blessing of the Forge}} completely removes the second effect of {{C|Armaments}} for respectively that combat or that hand. Similarly, other sources of {{KW|Upgrade|Upgrades}}, such as {{R|Warped Tongs}} and {{C|Lesson Learned}} can reduce the effectiveness of this card.\n** Having {{C|Searing Blow}} causes an exception to this, as it can still be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} by {{C|Armaments}} even if {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} before.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] shows three in-game [[Relics]]: {{R|Vajra}}, {{R|Champion Belt}}, and {{R|Lantern}}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed Armaments card not updating descriptions of upgraded cards.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Using more noticeable flashy VFX for cards upgraded via Armaments or Warped Tongs.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 36: Power Through'''\n** Draw and Discard piles can now be opened from hand select screen (Gambling Chip, Armaments, etc).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Previewing cards via Armaments wasn't applying powers. Fixed.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Armaments' upgrade preview now displays values based on Powers applied to you.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1944":{"pageid":1944,"ns":0,"title":"Backflip","revisions":[{"revid":56770,"parentid":56769,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Backflip\n| Image       = Green-Backflip.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain (5;8) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Draw 2 cards.\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw, Block\n}}\n{{C|Backflip}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 5 (8 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and draws 2 cards.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2437":{"pageid":2437,"ns":0,"title":"Bandage Up","revisions":[{"revid":56892,"parentid":50718,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Bandage Up\n|Image       = Colorless-BandageUp.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Heal (4;6) HP.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Exhaust, Heal\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Bandage Up}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It heals 4 (6 if upgraded) HP, and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Obtaining Bandage Up ==\n{{C|Bandage Up}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Magic Flower}} increases the effectiveness of the healing.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Healing cards cannot be generated mid-combat to avoid infinite healing, so {{C|Bandage Up}} cannot be created by {{C|Distraction}}, {{C|Chrysalis}} or {{R|Dead Branch}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Bandage Up now has upgrade functionality (4HP -> 6 HP)\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2378":{"pageid":2378,"ns":0,"title":"Become Almighty","revisions":[{"revid":53299,"parentid":50767,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"#REDIRECT [[Wish#Become Almighty]]"}}}]},"2267":{"pageid":2267,"ns":0,"title":"Bowling Bash","revisions":[{"revid":55666,"parentid":50635,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Bowling Bash\n|Image       = Purple-BowlingBash.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (7;10) damage for each enemy in combat.\n}}\n{{C|Bowling Bash}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (10 if upgraded) damage, for an amount of times equal to the amount of enemies in combat, to one target.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits once from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}} per hit, so for every enemy in combat.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Only currently alive enemies count for this card, meaning dead {{M|Darkling|Darklings}} do not count.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* When this card is played while 3 or more enemies are present, a sound of bowling pins falling will play.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2441":{"pageid":2441,"ns":0,"title":"Dark Shackles","revisions":[{"revid":56957,"parentid":55724,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Dark Shackles\n|Image       = Colorless-DarkShackles.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Enemy loses (9;15) {{BD|Strength}} this turn.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Shackled, Strength (Negative)\n|GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Shackled}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Dark Shackles}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It applies '''negative''' 9 (15 if upgraded) {{BD|Strength}} to the target, and gives them the same amount of {{BD|Shackled}} to regain that missing {{BD|Strength}} at the end of their turn. {{C|Dark Shackles}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Obtaining Dark Shackles ==\n{{C|Dark Shackles}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* The {{M|The Champ}}, the {{M|Awakened One}} and the {{M|Time Eater}} clear [[Debuff]s] when they are about to enter their second phase, meaning the {{BD|Strength}} penalty is maintained while {{BD|Shackled}} is removed. This means they get the {{BD|Strength}} penalty permanently instead of just that turn.\n** However, if this causes them to have '''negative''' {{BD|Strength}}, this will also be considered a [[Debuff]] and will be removed, leaving them with 0 {{BD|Strength}}.\n* The {{M|Corrupt Heart}} clears ''only'' '''negative''' {{BD|Strength}} when they buff (except for the turn 1 buff), meaning the {{BD|Strength}} penalty is removed but the {{BD|Shackled}} is maintained. This means it will permanently gain that amount of {{BD|Strength}} at the end of their turn.\n* {{C|Dark Shackles}} applies two effects per enemy: a [[Debuff]] to remove the {{BD|Strength}}, and {{BD|Shackled}} to add it back at end of turn. Despite this, enemies with {{BD|Artifact}} will still just lose one stack to negate the negative {{BD|Strength}}, without receiving the {{BD|Shackled}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 48: Creative AI'''\n** Certain enemies no longer gain extra strength when removing Piercing Wail or Dark Shackles from themselves.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 9: Ascension'''\n** Sadistic Nature no longer triggers twice from Shackles and Piercing Wail.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Dark Shackles+. -9 Str -> -15 Str\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!'''\n** Enemies that remove debuffs no longer keep the str gain portion of Piercing Wail/Dark Shackles.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Fixed rare crash for Dark Shackles card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Dark Shackles now has a period in its description.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1953":{"pageid":1953,"ns":0,"title":"Decay","revisions":[{"revid":56777,"parentid":55734,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Decay\n|Image       = Curse-Decay.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Curse\n|Cost        = -2\n|NoUpgrade   = true\n|Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>At the end of your turn, take 2 damage.\n|GivesToPlayer = Unplayable\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}}\n{{C|Decay}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. If it is in your hand at end of turn, it will [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] itself, and deal 2 damage to you.\n\n== Obtaining Decay ==\nLike most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, Decay can be obtained from anything that gives a random Curse:\n* Can be part of Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a reward.\n* {{E|Match and Keep}}.\n* {{R|Cursed Key}}.\n* {{KW|Transform|Transforming}} another Curse.\n\nIn addition, Decay can be obtained from the {{E|Forgotten Altar}} and {{E|Wheel of Change}} [[Events]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Decay will discard itself at the end of your turn before the rest of your hand, at the same time it applies the damage. This happens ''before'' {{KW|Retain}} happens, so you cannot choose to Retain it.\n<!--- I'm just including the main extra interactions here, but with the ones not relevant to the current page commented away. This allows easy transfer to related pages.--->\n* Decay, {{C|Burn|Burns}}, {{C|Shame}}, {{C|Doubt}}, and {{C|Regret}} all activate at the same time at end of turn. Visually they activate from left to right. However:\n** Regardless of the order of activation, {{C|Regret}} counts any copies of the others as being still in your hand when its damage is applied.\n<!---*** {{C|Regret}} does ''not'' take into account cards drawn from {{R|Runic Cube}} as a result of taking damage from these cards; it will always just use the number of cards in your hand when your turn ended.--->\n** If Decay, {{C|Regret}}, or {{C|Burn}} cause you to draw into any of the above via {{R|Runic Cube}}, those newly drawn cards will ''not'' go off, and will be discarded with the rest of your hand.\n** The damage for Decay, {{C|Burn}}, and {{C|Regret}} are applied from left to right. So, if you have 1 stack of {{BD|Buffer}} and two of them in hand, the left one will have its damage consumed, and the right one will apply.\n*** When selecting cards from your hand, such as to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] or {{KW|Exhaust}}, you can freely reorder your hand, as selecting and then unselecting a card moves it to the last spot in your hand. If needed, this can be used to manipulate which card's damage is applied to you.\n<!---** For Shame and {{C|Doubt}}, the {{KW|Debuff|Debuffs}} are applied from left to right. So, if you have 1 stack of {{BD|Artifact}} and both in hand, the left one will consume the Artifact and the right one will apply.\n*** When selecting cards from your hand, such as to {{KW|Discard}} or {{KW|Exhaust}}, you can freely reorder your hand, as selecting and then unselecting a card moves it to the last spot in your hand. If needed, this can be used to manipulate which Curse's debuff is applied to you.--->\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAs Decay is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you 1 {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for 1 HP. \n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you 6 max HP if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' Omamori.\n\nThe damage dealt with Decay can be:\n* Negated with {{BD|Buffer}}, via {{R|Fossilized Helix}} and {{C|Buffer}}.\n* Reduced to 1 with {{BD|Intangible}}, via {{R|Incense Burner}}, {{C|Wraith Form}}, and {{C|Apparition}}.\n* Reduced by 1 with {{R|Tungsten Rod}}.\nHowever, as Decay only does 2 damage and can be blocked, these are generally not needed.\n\nThe damage dealt by Decay can also be used to your benefit if it causes you to lose HP:\n* Losing HP causes {{R|Runic Cube}} to draw you a card.\n* {{C|Blood for Blood}} will have its cost reduced for the rest of combat.\n* The HP loss is counted as being from a card, so {{C|Rupture}} will gain you {{BD|Strength}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* As Decay deals damage rather than causing HP loss directly, it can be prevented with {{KW|Block}}, unlike {{C|Regret}} and {{C|Pain}}.\n* Decay generally cannot be {{KW|Retain|Retained}}, and does not stay in your hand with {{R|Runic Pyramid}}, as it discards itself as part of its end of turn activation.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as Decay, it cannot be played.\n* If the damage dealt by Decay causes you to lose HP, {{C|Masterful Stab}} will have its cost increased for the rest of combat.\n\n== Trivia ==\nDecay can be seen as the Curse equivalent of the {{C|Burn}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}}. Both deal 2 damage to you at end of turn, and their end of turn interactions are identical.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2037":{"pageid":2037,"ns":0,"title":"Doppelganger","revisions":[{"revid":55746,"parentid":53376,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Doppelganger\n|Image       = Green-Doppelganger.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = -1\n|Description = Next turn, draw (X;X+1) cards and gain (X;X+1) {{Icon|GE}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Draw, Energy\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Draw Card}}{{Power Infobox|Energized (Silent)}}\n{{C|Doppelganger}} is an X {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives X (X+1 if upgraded) {{BD|Draw Card}}, which draws that amount of cards at the start of your next turn, and X (X+1 if upgraded) {{BD|Energized (Silent)}}, which gives you that amount of extra {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' at the start of your next turn.\n\nWhen playing an X {{Icon|GE}}-cost card, all {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' that you currently have will be consumed. The {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' consumed this way will be used as the value for X.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Chemical X}} makes {{C|Doppelganger}} apply 2 more times, regardless of the amount of {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' used to play it.\n* If played using {{P|Distilled Chaos}}, {{C|Havoc}}, or {{C|Omniscience}}, it will play for the full current {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' without actually using any.\n* Can be used with 0 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' to advance {{R|Ink Bottle}} or {{R|Letter Opener}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If {{C|Doppelganger}} is duplicated with an effect such as a {{P|Duplication Potion}} or {{C|Burst}}, the value of X will also be used for the copy.\n* Being an X-cost, {{C|Doppelganger}} can be targeted by {{C|Recycle}} to double the current {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy'''.\n* It will not count as a 0-cost card for {{C|Scrape}} or {{C|All for One}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Corruption and other cost reducing cards no longer make X cost cards like Transmutation and Malaise display cost 0.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Removing 'Spend all [R].' from all X-cost cards for consistency.\n** Fixed bug where cost X cards do not work with energy gain cards if played too fast.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1922":{"pageid":1922,"ns":0,"title":"Doubt","revisions":[{"revid":56748,"parentid":55748,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Doubt\n| Image       = Curse-Doubt.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Curse\n| Cost        = -2\n| NoUpgrade   = true\n| Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>At the end of your turn, gain 1 {{BD|Weak}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Weak, Unplayable\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}} {{Power Infobox|Weak}}\n{{C|Doubt}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. If it is in your hand at end of turn, it will [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] itself, and apply 1 {{BD|Weak}} to you.\n\n== Obtaining Doubt ==\nLike most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, Doubt can be obtained from anything that gives a random Curse:\n* Can be part of Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a reward.\n* {{E|Match and Keep}}.\n* {{R|Cursed Key}}.\n* {{KW|Transform|Transforming}} another Curse.\n\nIn addition, Doubt can be obtained from {{E|The Ssssserpent}} Event when choosing {{Frame|Agree}} as well as {{E|Mind Bloom}} when choosing {{Frame|I am Healthy}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Doubt will discard itself at the end of your turn before the rest of your hand, at the same time it applies the {{BD|Weak}}. This happens ''before'' {{KW|Retain}} happens, so you cannot choose to Retain it.\n<!--- I'm just including the main extra interactions here, but with the ones not relevant to the current page commented away. This allows easy transfew to related pages.--->\n* Doubt, {{C|Shame}}, {{C|Regret}}, {{C|Decay}}, and {{C|Burn|Burns}} all activate at the same time at end of turn. Visually they activate from left to right. However:\n** Regardless of the order of activation, {{C|Regret}} counts any copies of the others as being still in your hand when its damage is applied.\n<!---*** {{C|Regret}} does ''not'' take into account cards drawn from {{R|Runic Cube}} as a result of taking damage from these cards; it will always just use the number of cards in your hand when your turn ended.--->\n<!---** The damage for {{C|Decay}}, {{C|Burn}}, and {{C|Regret}} are applied from left to right. So, if you have 1 stack of {{BD|Buffer}} and two of them in hand, the left one will have its damage consumed, and the right one will apply.\n*** When selecting cards from your hand, such as to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] or {{KW|Exhaust}}, you can freely reorder your hand, as selecting and then unselecting a card moves it to the last spot in your hand. If needed, this can be used to manipulate which card's damage is applied to you.--->\n** For Doubt and {{C|Shame}}, the [[Debuffs]] are applied from left to right. So, if you have 1 stack of {{BD|Artifact}} and both in hand, the left one will consume the Artifact and the right one will apply.\n*** When selecting cards from your hand, such as to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] or {{KW|Exhaust}}, you can freely reorder your hand, as selecting and then unselecting a card moves it to the last spot in your hand. If needed, this can be used to manipulate which Curse's debuff is applied to you.\n=== Synergies ===\nAs Doubt is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you 1 {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for 1 HP. \n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you 6 max HP if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' Omamori.\n\nThe {{BD|Weak}} debuff can be dealt with in a few ways:\n* It can be prevented with sources of {{BD|Artifact}}, such as {{C|Core Surge}} and {{C|Panacea}}.\n* It can be removed during your next turn with {{R|Orange Pellets}}.\n* The downside can be ignored by having a damage plan that doesn't require {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards, such as {{C|Juggernaut}}, {{C|A Thousand Cuts}}, {{BD|Poison}}, {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}}, {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}}, or {{C|The Bomb}}.\n* {{R|Runic Pyramid}} and {{KW|Retain}} effects such as {{C|Well-Laid Plans}} can allow you to save your key Attacks for when the {{BD|Weak}} has cleared.\n* {{C|Vault}} can be used to skip to your next turn, clearing the debuff without giving the enemy a turn.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Doubt cannot be {{KW|Retain|Retained}}, and does not stay in your hand with {{R|Runic Pyramid}}, as it discards itself as part of its end of turn activation.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as Doubt, it cannot be played.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The beta design of Doubt is a reference to the Press X to Doubt meme.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1893":{"pageid":1893,"ns":0,"title":"Fiend Fire","revisions":[{"revid":56427,"parentid":55777,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Fiend Fire\n| Image       = Red-FiendFire.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = {{KW|Exhaust}} your hand.<br>Deal (7;10) damage for each card {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n| InteractsWith = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Fiend Fire}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} all cards in your hand, and deals 7 (10 if upgraded) damage for every card {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} this way, excluding itself. {{C|Fiend Fire}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* If you have {{R|Dead Branch}} and {{C|Dark Embrace}} and play {{C|Fiend Fire}} to {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} multiple cards, it resolves 1 card at a time. This means the order goes: \n# Your hand is fully {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}.\n# The 1st {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} card generates a new card via {{R|Dead Branch}}.\n# The 1st {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} card draws a card via {{C|Dark Embrace}}.\n# Moves onto the 2nd card, repeat steps 2 and 3.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Fiend Fire}} has {{KW|Exhaust}}-synergy with {{C|Dark Embrace}}, {{C|Feel No Pain}}, {{R|Charon's Ashes}} and {{R|Dead Branch}}, and can reliably {{KW|Exhaust}} {{C|Sentinel}}.\n* Benefits once from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}} per hit, so per card {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}.\n\n=== Neutral === \n* {{C|Fiend Fire}} only has an effect if it has cards to {{KW|Exhaust}}. This means that playing it twice using for example {{C|Double Tap}} or {{R|Necronomicon}} does nothing, unless the cards are replaced in between through {{C|Dark Embrace}} or {{R|Dead Branch}}.\n\n=== Trivia ===\n* {{C|Fiend Fire}} appears as a cameo in [https://foursouls.com/cards/rwz-fiend_fire/ The Binding of Isaac: Four Souls].\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2440":{"pageid":2440,"ns":0,"title":"Finesse","revisions":[{"revid":50725,"parentid":36926,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Finesse\n|Image       = Colorless-Finesse.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Gain (2;4) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Draw 1 card.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Finesse}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 2 (4 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}, and draws 1 card.\n\n== Obtaining Finesse ==\n{{C|Finesse}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Finesse+. 2 -> 4 Block.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1935":{"pageid":1935,"ns":0,"title":"Fire Breathing","revisions":[{"revid":56760,"parentid":55779,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Fire Breathing\n|Image       = Red-FireBreathing.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Whenever you draw a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} card, deal (6;10) damage to ALL enemies.\n|GivesToPlayer = Fire Breathing\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Fire Breathing\n|Image        = Icon FireBreathing.png\n|Description  = Whenever you draw a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} card, deal X damage to ALL enemies.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Intensity\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n|InteractsWith = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Fire Breathing}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 6 (10 if upgraded) {{BD|Fire Breathing}}, which deals that amount of damage whenever a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} card is drawn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Fire Breathing}} only activates upon {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} cards being drawn. This means that cards created in hand, such as through {{C|Power Through}}, do not trigger it. \n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fire Breathing card reworked.\n\n* ''Day 1 Patch''\n** Dropkick, Fire Breathing, and Shockwave portraits weren't rendering in card popup view.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1911":{"pageid":1911,"ns":0,"title":"Injury","revisions":[{"revid":56737,"parentid":55825,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Injury\n| Image       = Curse-Injury.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Curse\n| Cost        = -2\n| NoUpgrade   = true\n| Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Unplayable\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}}\n{{C|Injury}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card.\n\n== Obtaining Writhe ==\nLike most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, Injury can be obtained from anything that gives a random Curse:\n* Can be part of Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a reward.\n* {{E|Match and Keep}}.\n* {{R|Cursed Key}}.\n* {{KW|Transform|Transforming}} another Curse.\n\nIn addition, Injury can be obtained from the {{E|Golden Idol}} Event when choosing {{Frame|Take}} and then {{Frame|Outrun}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\nAs Injury is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you 1 {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for 1 HP. \n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you 6 max HP if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' Omamori.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as Injury, it cannot be played.\n\n== Trivia ==\nInjury can be seen as the Curse equivalent of the {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} {{C|Wound}}, with both being the most basic penalty cards of their respective types.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1529":{"pageid":1529,"ns":0,"title":"Limit Break","revisions":[{"revid":56356,"parentid":55840,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Limit Break\n| Image       = Red-LimitBreak.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Double your {{BD|Strength}}.(<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.;)\n| GivesToPlayer = Strength\n| InteractsWith = Strength\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Strength}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Limit Break}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It doubles the amount of {{BD|Strength}} you have. {{C|Limit Break}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself, if it is not upgraded.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Depends on {{BD|Strength}}, meaning it synergizes with sources of it:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Inflame}}, {{C|Rupture}}, {{C|Spot Weakness}}, {{C|Demon Form}}.\n* {{C|Flex}} gives temporary {{BD|Strength}}, but doubling it will effectively allow you to keep the original amount permanently.\n* {{C|J.A.X.}}.\n* {{C|Reprogram}}.\n* {{C|Fasting}}, {{C|Wish}}.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Brimstone}}, {{R|Du-Vu Doll}}, {{R|Girya}},  {{R|Red Skull}}, {{R|Shuriken}}, {{R|Sling of Courage}}, {{R|Vajra}}. \n* {{R|Mutagenic Strength}} gives temporary {{BD|Strength}}, but doubling it will effectively allow you to keep the original amount permanently.\n==== c) Potions ====\n* {{P|Strength Potion}}, {{P|Cultist Potion}}.\n* {{P|Flex Potion}} gives temporary {{BD|Strength}}, but doubling it will effectively allow you to keep the original amount permanently.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{C|Limit Break}} will have no effect if you have 0 {{BD|Strength}} when played, but will still {{KW|Exhaust}} if not {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* This card also doubles negative {{BD|Strength}}. \n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 36: Power Through'''\n** Limit Break card now also doubles negative strength.\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Keywords for cards now cleared on upgrade (Limit break was showing exhaust tooltip post upgrade).\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2411":{"pageid":2411,"ns":0,"title":"Omniscience","revisions":[{"revid":55877,"parentid":54871,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Omniscience\n|Image       = Purple-Omniscience.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 4\n|CostPlus    = 3\n|Description = Choose a card in your draw pile.<br>Play the chosen card twice and {{KW|Exhaust}} it.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{C|Omniscience}} is a 4 (3 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It allows you to select one card in your draw pile, which it will play twice and {{KW|Exhaust}}, without expending any {{Icon|RE}}. Both copies of an X-cost card played this way will use the {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' you have after playing {{C|Omniscience}} for X, without consuming that {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''. {{C|Omniscience}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Using {{C|Omniscience}} to play another copy of {{C|Omniscience}} that is in your draw pile will result in 2 cards being played and doubled. {{C|Omniscience}} can be chained in this way to theorethically play your entire draw pile.\n* {{C|Omniscience}} increases the counter of {{BD|Time Warp}} as normal, but bypasses its forced end of turn. This means that if an {{C|Omniscience}} is played as the 12th card, its full effects, including a possible {{C|Omniscience}} chain, will take effect before your turn is ended.\n** However, playing an {{C|Omniscience}} as the 11th card and targeting a card that is not {{C|Omniscience}} will result in only one copy of that card being played.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Since {{C|Indignation}} and {{C|Inner Peace}} both have different effects depending on your current {{KW|Stance}}, and both of them can put you into their respective {{KW|Stance}}, targeting either of these cards with {{C|Omniscience}} can result in two different effects happening.\n* Unlike {{BD|Time Warp}}, which forces an end of turn, {{C|Normality}} and {{R|Velvet Choker}} enforce a limit on the amount of cards played, which {{C|Omniscience}} cannot bypass. \n* {{R|Strange Spoon}} has a 50% chance of saving a card that would be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by {{C|Omniscience}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Targeting a card that ends your turn, such as {{C|Meditate}} or {{C|Vault}}, will end your turn after the first copy played and not play a second copy or any remaining cards of an {{C|Omniscience}} chain.\n* Targeting a card that requires certain conditions to be met for that card to have an effect, such as {{C|Signature Move}}, without meeting those requirements will result in the card being played and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}, but not in the effects of that card taking place.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1814":{"pageid":1814,"ns":0,"title":"Reflex","revisions":[{"revid":56373,"parentid":55484,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Reflex\n|Image       = Green-Reflex.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = -2\n|Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>If this card is discarded from your hand, draw (2;3) cards.\n|GivesToPlayer = Draw, Discard, Unplayable\n}}\n{{C|Reflex}} is an unplayable {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Reflex does nothing unless [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]], in one of the following ways:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Survivor}}, {{C|Acrobatics}}, {{C|Dagger Throw}}, {{C|Prepared}}, {{C|Calculated Gamble}}, {{C|Concentrate}}, {{C|Tools of the Trade}},{{C|Storm of Steel}}, {{C|Unload}}.\n* {{C|All-Out Attack}}, although this cannot reliably target {{C|Reflex}}.\n* {{C|Scrape}}.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Gambling Chip}}.\n* {{P|Gambler's Brew}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Under normal circumstances, Reflex is the only card in the game which can directly draw itself. Normally, cards don't go to the discard until ''after'' all of their effects have completed, so there's no way for a card to draw itself. However, Reflex is already in the discard by the time its effect goes off, so if there are few enough cards in the draw pile, it is possible to shuffle and immediately redraw it.\n** Other cards may draw themselves via secondary effects like {{R|Ink Bottle}} going off, but only Reflex can do so only through its own effect.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Reflex card buffed. Card draw increased from 1 -> 2.\n** Reflex+ card buffed. Card draw increased from 2 -> 3.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** We removed one level of unlocks! Three additional cards are now available by default in the card pool for both The Silent and Ironclad. The following cards are now added to the card pool by default: Underhanded Strike, Reflex, Tactician\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2119":{"pageid":2119,"ns":0,"title":"Reprogram","revisions":[{"revid":55922,"parentid":50601,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Reprogram\n|Image       = Blue-Reprogram.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Lose (1;2) {{BD|Focus}}. <br>Gain (1;2) {{BD|Strength}}. <br>Gain (1;2) {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Focus}}{{Power Infobox|Strength}}{{Power Infobox|Dexterity}}\n{{C|Reprogram}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. <!--It removes 1 (2) {{BD|Focus}}, but gains 1 (2) {{BD|Strength}} and 1 (2) {{BD|Dexterity}}.-->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies === \n* Once you start lowering {{BD|Focus}}, doing so more is generally much less of a downside, so Reprogram and {{C|Hyperbeam}} work well together.\n* {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}} do not benefit from {{BD|Focus}}, and are unaffected by its removal: {{C|Fusion}}, {{C|Meteor Strike}}, {{R|Nuclear Battery}}\n** {{C|Chaos}} can also produce {{KW|Plasma}}, but is much more likely to produce Orbs affected by the {{BD|Focus}} loss.\n\n* As Reprogram is the only {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} card to directly produce {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Dexterity}}, it is particularly useful for a number of [[Defect|Defect's]] non-Orb cards:\n** 0-cost strategies using {{C|Scrape}} and {{C|All for One}} tend to play lots of cheap cards which provide damage and {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{C|Rip and Tear}} and {{C|Reinforced Body}} hit and {{KW|Block}} multiple times, benefiting extra from the {{BD|Strength}} and {{BD|Dexterity}}. {{C|Barrage}} may similarly benefit, but is often less useful as the negative {{BD|Focus}} makes [[Orbs]] less useful.\n\n* {{C|Core Surge}}, {{C|Panacea}}, {{R|Clockwork Souvenir}}, and {{R|Orange Pellets}} may all be used to prevent/remove the {{BD|Focus}} loss of Reprogram, allowing it to be used without affecting your Orbs.\n** Note that {{R|Orange Pellets}} can only clear negative {{BD|Focus}}, and it will not fix Reprogram taking away positive {{BD|Focus}}.\n\n* If a character other than [[The Defect]] manages to get Reprogram, such as from {{R|Prismatic Shard}}, the downside is essentially eliminated.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Focus}} only affects the future growth of {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}}, minimizing the effect of Reprogram on them later in combats.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Reprogram reduces the effectiveness of sources that add {{BD|Focus}}: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Reprogram also weakens all non-{{KW|Plasma}} Orb sources, such as {{C|Ball Lightning}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}.\n** As a secondary effect of this, many Orb-related cards do not work well with Reprogram, such as {{C|Compile Driver}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Reprogram card Focus loss decreased from 2 -> 1.\n** Reprogram+ card changed. Focus loss, Strength, and Dexterity changed from 1 -> 2.\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Reprogram card reworked.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 31: Custom Mode'''\n** Optional UPGRADE_DESCRIPTION added for Pummel, Heavy Blade, Offering, and Reprogram\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2417":{"pageid":2417,"ns":0,"title":"Spirit Shield","revisions":[{"revid":50709,"parentid":36439,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Spirit Shield\n|Image       = Purple-SpiritShield.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Gain (3;4) {{KW|Block}} for each card in your hand.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{C|Spirit Shield}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 3 (4 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} multiplied by the amount of cards in hand.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1818":{"pageid":1818,"ns":0,"title":"Unload","revisions":[{"revid":56375,"parentid":55521,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Unload\n|Image       = Green-Unload.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (14;18) damage.<br>Discard all non-Attack cards in your hand.\n|GivesToPlayer = Discard\n}}\n{{C|Unload}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 14 (18 if upgraded) damage, and [[Keywords#Discard|discards]] all non-{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards in your hand.\n\n== Interactions == \n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Unload}}'s [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] effect synergises with several [[Silent]] cards and relics: \n\n==== Cards ====\n* [[Keywords#Discard|Discarding]] {{C|Tactician}} or {{C|Reflex}} will immediately activate their effects.\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} is discounted by X {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' this turn, where X is the number of cards [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}} will now refund 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if also played this turn.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}} will grant 3 {{KW|Block}} per card [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{R|Tingsha}} will deal 3 damage to a random enemy per card [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{R|Hovering Kite}} will generate 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if this is the first time a card has been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] this turn.\n\n=== Neutral === \n* {{C|Unload}} can also be used to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] cards with end-of-turn effects, like {{C|Burn}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} such as {{C|Regret}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Unload card buff: Damage 12 -> 14. Upgraded 16 -> 18.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}